<section class="work-panel" id="fabrication-panel"><div class="panel-title"><h2>Proposed BBS · nominal bends and cuts</h2><button id="export-proposed-bbs" type="button">Download proposed BBS · CSV</button></div><div class="v3-section-body"><p class="v5-code-note">Review only. Nominal cuts exclude the unresolved hook closure offset; they are not fabrication instructions.</p><div id="proposal-status" aria-live="polite"></div><div id="confinement-check"></div><div id="proposed-bbs"></div><div class="v5-shape-controls"><label>Dimensioned bar shape<select id="shape-select"></select></label><button id="export-proposed-shape" type="button">Download shape · SVG</button></div><div id="fabrication-shape" class="v5-shape"></div><details><summary>Exact tangent and arc calculation</summary><div id="shape-segments"></div></details><details><summary>Lap fit, anchorage and material acceptance</summary><div id="lap-fit"></div><p>Source footing development of <strong>60φ</strong> and stair development of <strong>1,570 mm</strong> are retained. They are not replaced by a shorter generic lap. The proposed Fe500 basis requires actual mill/test properties; a Fe500D label alone does not establish the NBC tensile/yield ratio of at least 1.15.</p><p>No force model, soil/exposure survey, approved coupler product, concrete-bearing design or coordinated joint/footing cage is supplied. These gaps remain fabrication holds.</p></details><details><summary>Selected-member stock packing · shaped pieces only</summary><div id="stock-packing"></div></details><p><a href="./data/proposed-bbs.csv">All-member proposed BBS · CSV</a> · <a href="./data/member-checks.json">Proposed checks · JSON</a> · <a href="./design-basis.json">Decision basis · JSON</a></p><a class="contents-return" href="#page-contents">Contents ↑</a></div></section>
<section class="work-panel" id="renderer-check"><div class="panel-title"><h2>3D renderer and device check</h2><button id="run-3d-check" type="button">Run this device's 3D check</button></div><div class="v3-section-body"><p>This checks the renderer actually used by your browser. A successful vector fallback is a separate result from a WebGL pass. A GPU cannot be made available by selecting a code assumption.</p><div id="renderer-results" aria-live="polite"></div><div class="v5-button-row"><button id="test-context-loss" type="button">Test WebGL context loss</button><button id="retry-webgl" type="button">Retry WebGL</button><button id="download-renderer-report" type="button">Download device report · JSON</button></div><p>Context loss deliberately switches to the linked vector view and removes the abandoned canvas. Retry requests a new renderer. Current view, geometry and selection remain available. Device reports are downloaded locally; they are not uploaded.</p></div></section>
